# Kept out of the Comfy Registry archive, not out of git. Syntax is .gitignore's,
# and it layers on top of it -- anything git already ignores is excluded anyway.
#
# The bundle is what lands in someone's custom_nodes/, so the rule here is
# "would a user of the nodes ever open this file?". Development tooling would
# not; documentation would, so every .md and docs/img/ stays (README.md is the
# registry listing's own body, and it references those images).
#
# CONTRIBUTING.md ships while the tooling it describes does not. That is
# deliberate: it points readers at the GitHub repo, which is where anyone
# changing the code should be working from in the first place.

# The test suite -- the largest thing here, and of no use without a checkout.
tests/

# Slurm job scripts and the smoke/measurement tooling they run.
slurm/
scripts/

# CI.
.github/

# Editor and local scratch.
.vscode/
.idea/
